# model_table -- the single per-model definition file: every per-model *fact*
# (plus deliberate per-model policy overrides) lives here once; hardware bring-up
# comes from each camera's stock lower_half_init.sh (gen-lower-half.sh).
#
# Columns (whitespace-separated); a row here is a claim about real hardware.
#   model        model_suffix token: what /backup/init.sh sets and -m carries
#   sensor       MIPI driver basename; used only when one row names it (gc2053 is shared)
#   ring_offset  fshare ring control-header size (bytes); 0 = autodetect
#   ring_header  per-frame header bytes before payload; 0 = autodetect
#   high_w/h     real HIGH-channel (video1) encoder geometry, SPS-verified
#   ptz          yes/no -- real motorized pan/tilt base
#   high_bitrate HIGH-channel bitrate to pin (bps); 0/absent = follow the
#                controller's target (a deliberate per-model policy override,
#                e.g. y623's weak 2.4 GHz link). The encoder target and both
#                declared bitrates (Go client + bridge) are pinned together.
#
# A row here means we own the hardware and can bring it up. No row = conservative
# default (368/28, 2304x1296, no PTZ) + warning, never a silent guess.
y623     gc3003  368  28  2304  1296  no  2800000
h51ga    gc2053  368  28  1920  1080  yes
h52ga    gc2053  368  28  1920  1080  yes
r35gb    gc2053  0    0   1920  1080  yes
y291ga   gc2053  368  28  1920  1080  no
